Condition : 12 - Prior to the first event of the following calendar year (and no later than 1st February in any calendar year) during the operational life of the development, the applicant shall submit to and approve by the Local Planning Authority an annual ecological report covering the preceding calendar year.
The annual report shall include:
i. a schedule of all events that have taken place at the site during the reporting period under the permission, including the nature, date(s), duration, and approximate attendance of each event;
ii. Photo records and site conditions report for before, during and after the events held in the calendar year, and on conclusion of each year hereby approved shall, make provision for the landowner to complete the necessary remediation to return the site to its pre-event state as a minimum in accordance with the details set out in the submitted document and supporting information;
iii. A confirmation that the habitats and condition identified during the approved Ecological Appraisal report have been retained;
iv. Root Protection Area during live event days of set up, live and removal in that calendar year or other time frame that is agreed by the Local Planning Authority;
v. The biodiversity net gain in that calendar year or other time frame that is agreed by the Local Planning Authority.
Reason: To safeguard the appearance and character of Gunnersbury Park and the ecology, in accordance with the intention of the NPPF, London Plan Policy G4 and G6, and Policies CC4, GB1, GB2, GB7 and GB9 of the Local Plan.

Condition : 13 - A Phase 2 Ecological Management Plan shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority 6 months after the approval of the application.
The Ecological Management Plan shall incorporate:
i details of measures to protect breeding birds, nests and eggs from mortality/damage, injury and disturbance, including avoidance by timing and/or appropriate supervision;
ii details of the ecological clerk of works supervision to be put in place to monitor the set up and removal to ensure no impact on undiscovered or other unexpected faunal encounters;
iii an ecological parameters lighting plan;
iv details of the location and type of any ecological enhancement measures;
v details of how the enhancement measures will be monitored, managed and maintained, including birds, bats, the long- term design objectives, management or reporting responsibilities and maintenance schedules;
vi details of species surveys within and around the site
The development shall then be carried out in accordance with the approved details.
Reason: In the interests of nature conservation.

Condition : 18 - A Community Access Strategy shall be implemented to provide free tickets and access to members of the local community for each publicly ticketed event held under this permission and shall include the following:
�	A minimum of 0.5% of tickets sold for publicly ticketed events shall be made available free of charge to the residents of the local area (based on geographic eligibility) and local groups, charities and schools.
�	This allocation of tickets shall be distributed as follows: 70% shall be made available for residents of the local area, and 30% shall be made available to local community groups, charities and schools located within Hounslow and Ealing.
�	The allocation of tickets made available to residents of the local area shall be based on the following geographic eligibility criteria: tickets for Band 1 events shall be made available to residents within 1km of Model Farm Building (the point between the two arena areas), and tickets for Band 2 events shall be made available to residents within 500m of Model Farm Building (the point between the two arena areas).

Details of the allocation of tickets and the take up pursuant to the Community Access Strategy shall be incorporated within the Annual Monitoring Report under Condition 4, including the following:
1.	For each publicly ticketed event day held during the reporting period:
a)	the event name, date and maximum attendees;
b)	the total number of tickets available for sale;
c)	the number of free tickets and access opportunities made available;
d)	the number of free tickets and access opportunities taken up;
e)	the means and period over which these were promoted;
f)	the local community groups, organisations and/or categories of persons to whom the free tickets were made available; and

2.	The total number of tickets and access opportunities made available and taken up within the calendar year.

Reason: To ensure the local community will be benefited from the events.
